IMPORT prelude

-- Corporations Act 2001 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what a founder meets as director and shareholder of a proprietary
-- company, from registration to sale, and afterwards as a listed company's director and an angel investor.
--
-- SEAT: the founder-director and shareholder (Daniel, of Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd): "What must I do as a
-- director, and how may I raise and sell shares?" Every question below is phrased as he would ask it, on facts he could
-- state. Where a provision addresses the company, ASIC or the market operator, the question is what it means for him: what
-- his company must do, what he can be made liable for, what he may not do.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Registering a proprietary company: ss 45A(2) (small proprietary company), 112(1), 113(1), 114,
-- 117, 118(1), 201A(1); who is a director and who may be one: ss 9AC, 201B; the director identification number: ss
-- 1272B(1)(a), 1272C. Directors' duties: ss 180, 181, 182, 183, 184, and disclosure of a material personal interest, s
-- 191. Raising money: offers that need no disclosure document, s 708(1), (2), (3), (5), (8), (9), (11), (12) (with s 9
-- "professional investor" and "senior manager"), and the proprietary company's bar, s 113(3), (4). Shares: s 254A(2)
-- (preference shares) and s 254T (dividends). Share buy-backs, Part 2J.1 Division 2: ss 257A, 257B (the table, the
-- equal access scheme, the 10/12 limit, on-market buy-backs), 257C, 257D (with s 250MA), 257E, 257F, 257G, 257H, and the s
-- 9 definitions of selective, minimum holding and employee share buy-back. Groups and sale: ss 46, 50, 606(1), (1A), (3).
-- On a listed board: continuous disclosure ss 674(2), 674A(2), (3), (4); insider trading ss 1042A, 1042C, 1042D, 1043A.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 149, compilation date 19 September 2026, includes amendments to Act No. 87, 2026 (register id
-- C2026C00432), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00818.txt (the seven volumes joined).
-- Regulations: the Corporations Regulations 2001 are NOT deposited. The amounts they set are INPUTS: the s 708(8)(c) net
-- assets and gross income figures, and any figures prescribed in place of the s 45A(2) revenue, assets and employee
-- numbers.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Almost all of a seven-volume Act. In particular: the rest of s 708 ((7), (10), (13) to (21)), s 708AA and
-- s 708A; what a prospectus must contain, s 727 offences and liability for defective disclosure (Part 6D.3); Chapter 7
-- licensing; reductions of capital (Division 1 of Part 2J.1) and redemption of preference shares; s 254Y and s 259A beyond
-- the table; ASIC's s 257D(4) exemption; insolvent trading (s 588G) and creditor-defeating dispositions; related party
-- benefits (Chapter 2E); ss 47 to 49 (board control, what to disregard); relevant interest and voting power (ss 608 to 610,
-- taken as given percentages) and the s 611 exceptions (an input); Note 3 to s 606(1); the CSF rules (ss 113(2)(c), (d),
-- 201A(1A)); the insider trading exceptions in ss 1043B to 1043K (one input) and the s 1043M defences; s 1042G (an
-- officer's knowledge imputed to the company); company trading windows (not in the Act at all); every penalty (Schedule 3,
-- s 1311, s 1317E). The ASX Listing Rules are not law in this repository: whether they require notification is an input.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Corporations Act 2001 -- the founder-director's questions`

§§ `ss 112, 113(1), 114, 117, 118, 201A -- registering my proprietary company`

-- s 117(1): "To register a company, a person must lodge an application with ASIC." (2): it "must state" (a) the type of
-- company; (b) the proposed name (unless the ACN is to be used); (c) "the name and address of each person who consents to
-- become a member"; (d), (f) the names, date and place of birth and address of each person who consents in writing to
-- become a director; (g) the proposed registered office; (k) for a company limited by shares, the number and class of
-- shares each member agrees in writing to take up and the amount each agrees to pay; (ma) whether there will be an
-- ultimate holding company; (n) the State or Territory. (4): "The application must be in the prescribed form." (5): "An
-- applicant must have the consents and agreements referred to in subsection (2) when the application is lodged." Items
-- (e), (h), (j), (l), (m), (mb) apply only to a secretary, a public company, a separate place of business, a guarantee
-- company or a company with a holding company, and are not asked.
DECLARE Application HAS
    `states the type of company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the proposed name or uses the ACN` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states each member's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states each director's names, date and place of birth and address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the shares each member agrees to take up and pay for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states whether there will be an ultimate holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold the written consents and agreements` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 112(1): a proprietary company is "Limited by shares" or "Unlimited with share capital". s 113(1): "A company must have
-- no more than 50 non-employee shareholders if it is to ... be registered as a proprietary company"; (2)(a) "count joint
-- holders of a particular parcel of shares as 1 person". s 114: "A company needs to have at least 1 member." s 201A(1):
-- "A proprietary company must have at least 1 director. That director must ordinarily reside in Australia."
DECLARE Company HAS
    `is limited by shares or unlimited with a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `non-employee shareholders, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER
    `members` IS A NUMBER
    `directors` IS A NUMBER
    `directors who ordinarily reside in Australia` IS A NUMBER

@export Does my application to register a company state everything s 117 requires?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc What your application to ASIC states, and whether you hold the members' and directors' written consents
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application meet s 117` IF
        `my application`'s `states the type of company`
    AND `my application`'s `states the proposed name or uses the ACN`
    AND `my application`'s `states each member's name and address`
    AND `my application`'s `states each director's names, date and place of birth and address`
    AND `my application`'s `states the registered office`
    AND `my application`'s `states the shares each member agrees to take up and pay for`
    AND `my application`'s `states whether there will be an ultimate holding company`
    AND `my application`'s `states the State or Territory`
    AND `my application`'s `is in the prescribed form`
    AND `my application`'s `I hold the written consents and agreements`

-- s 118(1): "If an application is lodged under section 117, ASIC may" give an ACN, register the company and issue a
-- certificate. The Act gives ASIC a discretion, not a duty, so the answer is that ASIC MAY register, never that it must.
@export Can my company be registered as a proprietary company, if ASIC decides to register it (ss 112, 113(1), 114, 117, 118, 201A)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc What your application to ASIC states
      `my company` IS A Company @desc The company as it will be on registration: its type, shareholders, members and directors
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my company be registered as a proprietary company` IF
        `Does my application meet s 117` `my application`
    AND `my company`'s `is limited by shares or unlimited with a share capital`
    AND `my company`'s `non-employee shareholders, joint holders counted as one` AT MOST 50
    AND `my company`'s `members` AT LEAST 1
    AND `my company`'s `directors` AT LEAST 1
    AND `my company`'s `directors who ordinarily reside in Australia` AT LEAST 1

§§ `s 45A(2) -- is my company a small proprietary company`

-- s 45A(2): "A proprietary company is a small proprietary company for a financial year if it satisfies at least 2 of the
-- following paragraphs: (a) the consolidated revenue ... is less than $25 million, or any other amount prescribed by the
-- regulations ...; (b) the value of the consolidated gross assets at the end of the financial year ... is less than $12.5
-- million, or any other amount prescribed ...; (c) the company and the entities it controls (if any) have fewer than 50,
-- or any other number prescribed ..., employees at the end of the financial year." (5): part-time employees count "as an
-- appropriate fraction of a full-time equivalent". (3): a LARGE proprietary company meets at least 2 of the opposite tests,
-- so with three tests a proprietary company is always exactly one of the two.
-- The thresholds are INPUTS: the Act's figures apply only if the regulations prescribe no other, and the regulations
-- are not deposited.
GIVEN `consolidated revenue` IS A NUMBER, `consolidated gross assets` IS A NUMBER, `full-time equivalent employees` IS A NUMBER, `revenue threshold` IS A NUMBER, `gross assets threshold` IS A NUMBER, `employee threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many of the s 45A(2) tests are met` MEANS
        (IF `consolidated revenue` LESS THAN `revenue threshold` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `consolidated gross assets` LESS THAN `gross assets threshold` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `full-time equivalent employees` LESS THAN `employee threshold` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

@export Is my proprietary company a small proprietary company for the financial year (s 45A(2))?
GIVEN `consolidated revenue` IS A NUMBER @desc Revenue for the financial year of the company and the entities it controls, in dollars
      `consolidated gross assets` IS A NUMBER @desc Consolidated gross assets at the end of the financial year, in dollars
      `full-time equivalent employees` IS A NUMBER @desc Employees of the company and the entities it controls at year end, part-timers as a fraction
      `revenue threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The revenue figure in force: $25,000,000 in the Act unless the regulations prescribe another
      `gross assets threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross assets figure in force: $12,500,000 in the Act unless the regulations prescribe another
      `employee threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee number in force: 50 in the Act unless the regulations prescribe another
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my company a small proprietary company` IF
    `how many of the s 45A(2) tests are met` `consolidated revenue` `consolidated gross assets` `full-time equivalent employees` `revenue threshold` `gross assets threshold` `employee threshold` AT LEAST 2

§§ `ss 9AC, 201B, 1272B, 1272C -- am I a director, and do I need a director identification number`

-- s 9AC(1): a DIRECTOR is "(a) a person who: (i) is appointed to the position of a director; or (ii) is appointed to the
-- position of an alternate director and is acting in that capacity ...; and (b) unless the contrary intention appears, a
-- person who is not validly appointed as a director if: (i) they act in the position of a director; or (ii) the directors
-- of the company or body are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's instructions or wishes (excluding advice
-- given by the person in the proper performance of functions attaching to the person's professional capacity or their
-- business relationship with the directors or the corporation)."
-- s 201B(1): "Only an individual who is at least 18 may be appointed as a director of a company." (2): a person
-- disqualified under Part 2D.6 only with ASIC's permission (s 206GAB) or the Court's leave (s 206G).
-- s 1272B(1)(a): an ELIGIBLE OFFICER is a director who "(i) is appointed to the position of a director; or (ii) is
-- appointed to the position of an alternate director and is acting in that capacity". A de facto director is not one.
-- s 1272C(1): "An eligible officer must have a director identification number." (2): not if the officer applied before
-- the day they first became an eligible officer (or within a period the regulations specify or the Registrar allows) and
-- the application "and any reviews arising out of it, have not been finally determined"; (3): not if "the officer became an
-- eligible officer without the officer's knowledge". (4): strict liability.
DECLARE Me HAS
    `my age` IS A NUMBER
    `I was appointed a director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was appointed an alternate director and am acting as one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I act in the position of a director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the directors are accustomed to act on my instructions or wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that is only advice given in my professional capacity or business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am disqualified from managing corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have ASIC's permission or the Court's leave` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a director identification number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I applied in time and the application is not yet finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I became an eligible officer without knowing it` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I a director of the company, appointed or not (s 9AC)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Me @desc Your position in the company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a director` IF
        `me`'s `I was appointed a director`
    OR  `me`'s `I was appointed an alternate director and am acting as one`
    OR  `me`'s `I act in the position of a director`
    OR  (    `me`'s `the directors are accustomed to act on my instructions or wishes`
         AND (NOT `me`'s `that is only advice given in my professional capacity or business relationship`))

@export May I be appointed a director (s 201B)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Me @desc Your age and any disqualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be appointed a director` IF
        `me`'s `my age` AT LEAST 18
    AND (    (NOT `me`'s `I am disqualified from managing corporations`)
         OR  `me`'s `I have ASIC's permission or the Court's leave`)

@export Am I an eligible officer who must have a director identification number (s 1272B(1)(a))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Me @desc Your position in the company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an eligible officer` IF
        `me`'s `I was appointed a director`
    OR  `me`'s `I was appointed an alternate director and am acting as one`

@export Am I in breach of the requirement to have a director identification number (s 1272C)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Me @desc Your position and whether you have, or have applied for, a director identification number
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in breach of the director ID requirement` IF
        `Am I an eligible officer` `me`
    AND (NOT `me`'s `I have a director identification number`)
    AND (NOT `me`'s `I applied in time and the application is not yet finally determined`)
    AND (NOT `me`'s `I became an eligible officer without knowing it`)

§§ `ss 180 to 184 -- my duties as a director`

-- s 180(1): "A director or other officer of a corporation must exercise their powers and discharge their duties with the
-- degree of care and diligence that a reasonable person would exercise if they: (a) were a director or officer of a
-- corporation in the corporation's circumstances; and (b) occupied the office held by, and had the same responsibilities
-- within the corporation as, the director or officer."
-- s 180(2) THE BUSINESS JUDGMENT RULE: one "who makes a business judgment is taken to meet the requirements of subsection
-- (1), and their equivalent duties at common law and in equity, in respect of the judgment if they: (a) make the judgment
-- in good faith for a proper purpose; and (b) do not have a material personal interest in the subject matter of the
-- judgment; and (c) inform themselves about the subject matter of the judgment to the extent they reasonably believe to be
-- appropriate; and (d) rationally believe that the judgment is in the best interests of the corporation. The ... belief
-- ... is a rational one unless the belief is one that no reasonable person in their position would hold."
-- s 180(3): "business judgment means any decision to take or not take action in respect of a matter relevant to the
-- business operations of the corporation." The Note: the rule protects s 180 and its general-law equivalents ONLY.
DECLARE Judgment HAS
    `it was a decision about the business operations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I made it in good faith for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had a material personal interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I informed myself as far as I reasonably believed appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I believed it was in the company's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable person in my position could hold that belief` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does the business judgment rule protect my decision (s 180(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my decision` IS A Judgment @desc The decision you made as a director and how you made it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the business judgment rule protect my decision` IF
        `my decision`'s `it was a decision about the business operations`
    AND `my decision`'s `I made it in good faith for a proper purpose`
    AND (NOT `my decision`'s `I had a material personal interest in it`)
    AND `my decision`'s `I informed myself as far as I reasonably believed appropriate`
    AND `my decision`'s `I believed it was in the company's best interests`
    AND `my decision`'s `a reasonable person in my position could hold that belief`

-- Whether a reasonable director in the company's circumstances would have acted as I did is a judgment the Act leaves to
-- the court: it is asked conditionally. The business judgment rule is a deeming: if it applies, the duty is met.
@export Have I met my duty of care and diligence as a director (s 180)?
GIVEN `my decision` IS A Judgment @desc The decision you made as a director and how you made it
      `if a court finds I used a reasonable director's care and diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you used the care and diligence of a reasonable person in your office and the company's circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met my duty of care and diligence` IF
        `if a court finds I used a reasonable director's care and diligence`
    OR  `Does the business judgment rule protect my decision` `my decision`

-- s 181(1): "A director or other officer of a corporation must exercise their powers and discharge their duties: (a) in
-- good faith in the best interests of the corporation; and (b) for a proper purpose."
@export Have I breached my duty to act in good faith and for a proper purpose (s 181(1))?
GIVEN `I acted in good faith in the company's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted honestly in what you believed were the company's best interests
      `I acted for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used your powers for the purposes for which they were given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I breached my duty of good faith` IF
        (NOT `I acted in good faith in the company's best interests`)
    OR  (NOT `I acted for a proper purpose`)

-- s 182(1): "A director, secretary, other officer or employee of a corporation must not improperly use their position to:
-- (a) gain an advantage for themselves or someone else; or (b) cause detriment to the corporation."
@export Have I improperly used my position in the company (s 182(1))?
GIVEN `I am a director, secretary, officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold one of those positions in the company
      `I used my position improperly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used your position in a way a reasonable person would see as improper
      `to gain an advantage for me or someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was to gain an advantage for you or anyone else
      `to cause the company detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was to cause the company detriment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I improperly used my position` IF
        `I am a director, secretary, officer or employee`
    AND `I used my position improperly`
    AND (`to gain an advantage for me or someone else` OR `to cause the company detriment`)

-- s 183(1): "A person who obtains information because they are, or have been, a director or other officer or employee of
-- a corporation must not improperly use the information to: (a) gain an advantage for themselves or someone else; or (b)
-- cause detriment to the corporation." Note 1: "This duty continues after the person stops being an officer or employee".
@export Have I improperly used information I got as a director, officer or employee, even after leaving (s 183(1))?
GIVEN `I got it because I am or was a director, officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained the information because of your present or past position
      `I used it improperly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used the information improperly
      `to gain an advantage for me or someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was to gain an advantage for you or anyone else
      `to cause the company detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was to cause the company detriment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I improperly used company information` IF
        `I got it because I am or was a director, officer or employee`
    AND `I used it improperly`
    AND (`to gain an advantage for me or someone else` OR `to cause the company detriment`)

-- s 184(1): a director or other officer "commits an offence if they: (a) are reckless; or (b) are dishonest; and fail to
-- exercise their powers and discharge their duties: (c) in good faith in the best interests of the corporation; or (d) for
-- a proper purpose." (2): a director, officer or employee commits an offence "if they use their position dishonestly: (a)
-- with the intention of directly or indirectly gaining an advantage ... or causing detriment to the corporation; or (b)
-- recklessly as to whether" it may. (3): the same for information obtained because of the position. (2A), (4): it is NOT a
-- defence that the advantage was intended for, or went to, the corporation -- so that fact is not asked.
@export Could I be guilty of a criminal offence under s 184 for how I acted as a director?
GIVEN `I was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were reckless
      `I was dishonest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were dishonest
      `I acted in good faith in the company's best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted in good faith in the company's best interests
      `I acted for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted for a proper purpose
      `I used my position dishonestly, meaning or risking an advantage or detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used your position dishonestly, intending or reckless as to an advantage for anyone or detriment to the company
      `I used company information dishonestly, meaning or risking an advantage or detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you used information obtained through your position dishonestly, intending or reckless as to an advantage or detriment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could I be guilty of an offence under s 184` IF
        (    (`I was reckless` OR `I was dishonest`)
         AND `Have I breached my duty of good faith` `I acted in good faith in the company's best interests` `I acted for a proper purpose`)
    OR  `I used my position dishonestly, meaning or risking an advantage or detriment`
    OR  `I used company information dishonestly, meaning or risking an advantage or detriment`

§§ `s 191 -- must I tell the other directors about my interest`

-- s 191(1): "A director of a company who has a material personal interest in a matter that relates to the affairs of the
-- company must give the other directors notice of the interest unless subsection (2) says otherwise." (2): no notice if
-- (a) the interest is one of eight listed kinds (held in common with the other members as a member; remuneration as a
-- director; a contract subject to members' approval; a guarantee or indemnity for a loan to the company; subrogation;
-- directors' insurance; a permitted indemnity; a contract with a related body corporate of which the director is a
-- director); (b) "the company is a proprietary company and the other directors are aware of the nature and extent of the
-- interest and its relation to the affairs of the company"; (c) notice was already given and "the nature or extent of the
-- interest has not materially increased"; (d) a standing notice under s 192 "is still effective". (3): notice "at a
-- directors' meeting as soon as practicable", recorded in the minutes. (4): a contravention does not affect validity.
-- (5): "This section does not apply to a proprietary company that has only 1 director."
DECLARE Interest HAS
    `I have a material personal interest in a matter of the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company is a proprietary company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `it is one of the kinds listed in s 191(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other directors know its nature and extent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I already gave notice and it has not materially increased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a standing notice under s 192 is still effective` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Must I give the other directors notice of my material personal interest (s 191)?
GIVEN `my interest` IS AN Interest @desc Your interest, the company and the board
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the other directors about my interest` IF
        `my interest`'s `I have a material personal interest in a matter of the company's affairs`
    AND (NOT (`my interest`'s `the company is a proprietary company` AND `my interest`'s `number of directors` EQUALS 1))
    AND (NOT `my interest`'s `it is one of the kinds listed in s 191(2)(a)`)
    AND (NOT (`my interest`'s `the company is a proprietary company` AND `my interest`'s `the other directors know its nature and extent`))
    AND (NOT `my interest`'s `I already gave notice and it has not materially increased`)
    AND (NOT `my interest`'s `a standing notice under s 192 is still effective`)

§§ `s 708, s 113(3) -- may my company raise money without a prospectus`

-- s 708(1): "Personal offers of a body's securities by a person do not need disclosure to investors under this Part if:
-- (a) none of the offers results in a breach of the 20 investors ceiling ...; and (b) none of the offers results in a
-- breach of the $2 million ceiling". (2): a PERSONAL OFFER "(a) may only be accepted by the person to whom it is made;
-- and (b) is made to a person who is likely to be interested in the offer, having regard to: (i) previous contact ...; or
-- (ii) some professional or other connection ...; or (iii) statements or actions by that person". (3): an issue breaches
-- a ceiling if it results in the number of people issued securities "exceeding 20 in any 12 month period", or the amount
-- raised "exceeding $2 million in any 12 month period". (5): in counting, "disregard issues and sales that result from
-- offers that: (a) do not need a disclosure document because of any other subsection of this section; or (b) are not
-- received in Australia; or (c) are made under a disclosure document."
-- s 708(8) SOPHISTICATED INVESTORS: no disclosure if "(a) the minimum amount payable for the securities on acceptance ...
-- is at least $500,000; or (b) the amount payable ... and the amounts previously paid by the person for the body's
-- securities of the same class that are held by the person add up to at least $500,000; or (c) it appears from a
-- certificate given by a qualified accountant no more than 6 months before the offer is made that the person ... (i) has
-- net assets of at least the amount specified in regulations ...; or (ii) has a gross income for each of the last 2
-- financial years of at least the amount specified in regulations ...; or (d) the offer is made to a company or trust
-- controlled by a person who meets" (c)(i) or (ii). (The certificate facts below may be the controller's, for (d).)
-- (9): "disregard any amount payable, or paid, to the extent to which it is to be paid, or was paid, out of money lent by
-- the person offering the securities or an associate."
-- s 708(11) PROFESSIONAL INVESTORS: no disclosure if made to "(a) a person covered by the definition of professional
-- investor in section 9 (except a person mentioned in paragraph (e) of the definition); or (b) a person who has or controls
-- gross assets of at least $10 million (including any assets held by an associate or under a trust that the person
-- manages)." (s 9 "professional investor" lists licensees, APRA-regulated bodies, listed entities and others: asked.)
-- s 708(12): no disclosure if made to "(a) a senior manager of the body or a related body or their spouse, parent, child,
-- brother or sister; or (b) a body corporate controlled by a person referred to in paragraph (a)." s 9: a SENIOR MANAGER
-- is "a person (other than a director or secretary of the corporation)" who makes or participates in making decisions
-- affecting the whole or a substantial part of the business, or can significantly affect its financial standing.
DECLARE Offer HAS
    `it may be accepted only by the person it is made to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are likely to be interested because of contact, a connection or their own statements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `people already issued securities in the last 12 months, as counted` IS A NUMBER
    `amount already raised in the last 12 months, as counted` IS A NUMBER
    `amount payable on acceptance` IS A NUMBER
    `amount they previously paid for same-class securities they still hold` IS A NUMBER
    `part paid out of money lent by the company or an associate` IS A NUMBER
    `there is a qualified accountant's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `whole months from the certificate to the offer` IS A NUMBER
    `further days from the certificate to the offer` IS A NUMBER
    `certified net assets` IS A NUMBER
    `certified gross income in each of the last 2 financial years` IS A NUMBER
    `they are a professional investor under s 9 other than by paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross assets they have or control` IS A NUMBER
    `they are a senior manager of the company or a related body, not a director or secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are a senior manager's spouse, parent, child, brother or sister, or a company one controls` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are an existing shareholder or an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is received in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is made under a disclosure document` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my company's offer of shares a personal offer (s 708(2))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer and the person it is made to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my offer a personal offer` IF
        `the offer`'s `it may be accepted only by the person it is made to`
    AND `the offer`'s `they are likely to be interested because of contact, a connection or their own statements`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is no more than 6 months old` IF
        `the offer`'s `there is a qualified accountant's certificate`
    AND (    `the offer`'s `whole months from the certificate to the offer` LESS THAN 6
         OR  (`the offer`'s `whole months from the certificate to the offer` EQUALS 6 AND `the offer`'s `further days from the certificate to the offer` EQUALS 0))

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount counted for s 708(8)(a)` MEANS
    `the offer`'s `amount payable on acceptance` MINUS `the offer`'s `part paid out of money lent by the company or an associate`

@export Is the person I am offering shares to a sophisticated investor, so that no disclosure is needed (s 708(8), (9))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer and the person it is made to
      `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The net assets figure set by the Corporations Regulations for s 708(8)(c)(i), in dollars (not deposited)
      `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The yearly gross income figure set by the Corporations Regulations for s 708(8)(c)(ii), in dollars (not deposited)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the investor a sophisticated investor for my offer` IF
        `the amount counted for s 708(8)(a)` `the offer` AT LEAST 500000
    OR  `the amount counted for s 708(8)(a)` `the offer` PLUS `the offer`'s `amount they previously paid for same-class securities they still hold` AT LEAST 500000
    OR  (    `the certificate is no more than 6 months old` `the offer`
         AND (    `the offer`'s `certified net assets` AT LEAST `the regulation net assets amount`
              OR  `the offer`'s `certified gross income in each of the last 2 financial years` AT LEAST `the regulation gross income amount`))

@export Is the person I am offering shares to a professional investor, so that no disclosure is needed (s 708(11))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer and the person it is made to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the investor a professional investor for my offer` IF
        `the offer`'s `they are a professional investor under s 9 other than by paragraph (e)`
    OR  `the offer`'s `gross assets they have or control` AT LEAST 10000000

@export Is my offer to a senior manager or a senior manager's close family, so that no disclosure is needed (s 708(12))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer and the person it is made to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my offer to a senior manager or their family` IF
        `the offer`'s `they are a senior manager of the company or a related body, not a director or secretary`
    OR  `the offer`'s `they are a senior manager's spouse, parent, child, brother or sister, or a company one controls`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER, `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer is exempt under another subsection` IF
        `Is the investor a sophisticated investor for my offer` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`
    OR  `Is the investor a professional investor for my offer` `the offer`
    OR  `Is my offer to a senior manager or their family` `the offer`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER, `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer is left out of the s 708(1) count` IF
        `the offer is exempt under another subsection` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`
    OR  (NOT `the offer`'s `it is received in Australia`)
    OR  `the offer`'s `it is made under a disclosure document`

@export Does my offer fall within the small-scale exemption: personal, and no more than 20 investors and $2 million in 12 months (s 708(1), (3), (5))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer, the person it is made to, and the issues already counted in the last 12 months
      `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 708(8)(c)(i) net assets figure from the regulations, in dollars
      `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 708(8)(c)(ii) gross income figure from the regulations, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my offer fall within the small-scale exemption` IF
        `Is my offer a personal offer` `the offer`
    AND (NOT `the offer is left out of the s 708(1) count` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`)
    AND `the offer`'s `people already issued securities in the last 12 months, as counted` PLUS 1 AT MOST 20
    AND `the offer`'s `amount already raised in the last 12 months, as counted` PLUS `the offer`'s `amount payable on acceptance` AT MOST 2000000

@export Does my company's offer of shares need a disclosure document such as a prospectus (s 708(1), (8), (11), (12))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer and the person it is made to
      `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 708(8)(c)(i) net assets figure from the regulations, in dollars
      `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 708(8)(c)(ii) gross income figure from the regulations, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my offer need a disclosure document` IF
        (NOT `the offer is exempt under another subsection` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`)
    AND (NOT `Does my offer fall within the small-scale exemption` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`)

-- s 113(3): "A proprietary company must not engage in any activity that would require disclosure to investors under
-- Chapter 6D, except for: (a) an offer of its shares ... to: (i) existing shareholders of the company; or (ii) employees of
-- the company or of a subsidiary of the company; or (b) a CSF offer." (3A): strict liability. (4): "An act or transaction
-- is not invalid merely because of a contravention" -- ASIC may require the company to become a public company (s 165).
@export Would my proprietary company break s 113(3) by making this offer?
GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer @desc The offer and the person it is made to
      `the regulation net assets amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 708(8)(c)(i) net assets figure from the regulations, in dollars
      `the regulation gross income amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 708(8)(c)(ii) gross income figure from the regulations, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would my proprietary company break s 113(3)` IF
        `Does my offer need a disclosure document` `the offer` `the regulation net assets amount` `the regulation gross income amount`
    AND (NOT `the offer`'s `they are an existing shareholder or an employee`)

§§ `ss 254A(2), 254T -- preference shares and dividends`

-- s 254A(2): "A company can issue preference shares only if the rights attached to the preference shares with respect to"
-- repayment of capital, participation in surplus assets and profits, dividends, voting, and priority "are set out in the
-- company's constitution (if any) or have been otherwise approved by special resolution of the company".
@export Can my company issue preference shares, for example to a Series A investor (s 254A(2))?
GIVEN `the rights are set out in the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the constitution sets out the shares' rights on capital, surplus, dividends, voting and priority
      `the rights were approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those rights were approved by a special resolution of members
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my company issue the preference shares` IF
    `the rights are set out in the constitution` OR `the rights were approved by special resolution`

-- s 254T(1): "A company must not pay a dividend unless: (a) the company's assets exceed its liabilities immediately before
-- the dividend is declared and the excess is sufficient for the payment of the dividend; and (b) the payment of the
-- dividend is fair and reasonable to the company's shareholders as a whole; and (c) the payment of the dividend does not
-- materially prejudice the company's ability to pay its creditors." This is the DIVIDEND test; a buy-back has its own.
@export May my company pay this dividend (s 254T)?
GIVEN `assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's assets immediately before the dividend is declared, in dollars, by the accounting standards
      `liabilities` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's liabilities at that time, in dollars
      `the dividend` IS A NUMBER @desc The total dividend, in dollars
      `it is fair and reasonable to the shareholders as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether paying it is fair and reasonable to the shareholders as a whole
      `it materially prejudices paying creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether paying it would materially prejudice the company's ability to pay its creditors
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my company pay the dividend` IF
        `assets` GREATER THAN `liabilities`
    AND `assets` MINUS `liabilities` AT LEAST `the dividend`
    AND `it is fair and reasonable to the shareholders as a whole`
    AND (NOT `it materially prejudices paying creditors`)

§§ `Part 2J.1 Division 2, ss 257A to 257H -- buying back shares`

-- s 9: "minimum holding buy-back means a buy-back of all of a holder's shares in a listed corporation if the shares are
-- less than a marketable parcel"; "employee share buy-back means a buy-back under a scheme that: (a) has as its purpose
-- the acquisition of shares ... by, or on behalf of" employees or salaried directors "and (b) has been approved by the
-- company in general meeting"; s 257B(6): an ON-MARKET buy-back "results from an offer made by a listed corporation on a
-- declared financial market in the ordinary course of trading" ((7), approved overseas markets, not encoded).
-- s 257B(2): an EQUAL ACCESS SCHEME "(a) the offers under the scheme relate only to ordinary shares; (b) the offers are to
-- be made to every person who holds ordinary shares to buy back the same percentage of their ordinary shares; (c) all of
-- those persons have a reasonable opportunity to accept the offers made to them; (d) buy-back agreements are not entered
-- into until a specified time for acceptances of offers has closed; (e) the terms of all the offers are the same."
-- s 9: "selective buy-back means a buy-back that is none of" those four.
DECLARE BuyBack IS ONE OF
    `minimum holding buy-back`
    `employee share buy-back`
    `on-market buy-back`
    `equal access scheme buy-back`
    `selective buy-back`

DECLARE BuyBackFacts HAS
    `the company is listed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it buys all of a holder's shares, less than a marketable parcel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is under an employee share scheme approved in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is made on a declared financial market in the ordinary course of trading` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offers relate only to ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every ordinary shareholder is offered the same percentage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `everyone has a reasonable opportunity to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no agreement is made until acceptances close` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms of all the offers are the same` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an equal access scheme` IF
        `the buy-back`'s `the offers relate only to ordinary shares`
    AND `the buy-back`'s `every ordinary shareholder is offered the same percentage`
    AND `the buy-back`'s `everyone has a reasonable opportunity to accept`
    AND `the buy-back`'s `no agreement is made until acceptances close`
    AND `the buy-back`'s `the terms of all the offers are the same`

@export What kind of buy-back is my company proposing (s 9, s 257B(2), (6))?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
GIVETH A BuyBack
DECIDE `What kind of buy-back is it` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buy-back`'s `the company is listed` AND `the buy-back`'s `it buys all of a holder's shares, less than a marketable parcel`
            THEN `minimum holding buy-back`
        IF `the buy-back`'s `it is under an employee share scheme approved in general meeting`
            THEN `employee share buy-back`
        IF `the buy-back`'s `the company is listed` AND `the buy-back`'s `it is made on a declared financial market in the ordinary course of trading`
            THEN `on-market buy-back`
        IF `it is an equal access scheme` `the buy-back`
            THEN `equal access scheme buy-back`
        OTHERWISE `selective buy-back`

-- s 257B(4): "The 10/12 limit ... is 10% of the smallest number, at any time during the last 12 months, of votes attaching
-- to voting shares of the company." (5): a proposed buy-back exceeds it if the votes attaching to the voting shares
-- "bought back during the last 12 months" and those "that will be bought back ... would exceed the 10/12 limit".
@export Would the buy-back exceed the 10/12 limit (s 257B(4), (5))?
GIVEN `smallest number of votes in the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The smallest number of votes attaching to voting shares at any time in the last 12 months
      `votes bought back in the last 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc Votes attaching to voting shares already bought back in the last 12 months
      `votes to be bought back` IS A NUMBER @desc Votes attaching to the voting shares this buy-back would buy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would the buy-back exceed the 10/12 limit` IF
    (`votes bought back in the last 12 months` PLUS `votes to be bought back`) TIMES 10 GREATER THAN `smallest number of votes in the last 12 months`

-- s 257B(1) THE TABLE, as data. Columns: minimum holding; employee share within / over the 10/12 limit; on-market within
-- / over; equal access scheme within / over; selective. Rows: "ordinary resolution [257C]" yes only for the three "over"
-- columns; "special/unanimous resolution [257D]" yes only for selective; "lodge offer documents with ASIC [257E]" yes for
-- both equal access columns and selective; "14 days notice [257F]" yes for all but minimum holding; "disclose relevant
-- information when offer made [257G]" yes for both equal access columns and selective; "cancel shares [257H]" and "notify
-- cancellation to ASIC [254Y]" yes for all. A selective buy-back has one column: the 10/12 limit does not matter to it.
DECLARE Steps HAS
    `ordinary resolution under s 257C` IS A BOOLEAN
    `special or unanimous resolution under s 257D` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lodge offer documents under s 257E` IS A BOOLEAN
    `14 days notice under s 257F` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclose relevant information with the offer under s 257G` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cancel the shares under s 257H` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notify ASIC of the cancellation under s 254Y` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the kind` IS A BuyBack, `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Steps
DECIDE `the s 257B steps for` IS
    --                                       257C                    257D   257E   257F   257G   257H  254Y
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `minimum holding buy-back`     THEN Steps OF FALSE,                   FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
    WHEN `employee share buy-back`      THEN Steps OF `over the 10/12 limit`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
    WHEN `on-market buy-back`           THEN Steps OF `over the 10/12 limit`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
    WHEN `equal access scheme buy-back` THEN Steps OF `over the 10/12 limit`, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE, TRUE
    WHEN `selective buy-back`           THEN Steps OF FALSE,                   TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE, TRUE

@export Must my company's members pass an ordinary resolution approving the buy-back (s 257B table, s 257C)?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
      `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would exceed the 10/12 limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my company pass an ordinary resolution for the buy-back` IF
    (`the s 257B steps for` (`What kind of buy-back is it` `the buy-back`) `over the 10/12 limit`)'s `ordinary resolution under s 257C`

@export Must my company's members pass a special or unanimous resolution approving the buy-back (s 257B table, s 257D)?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
      `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would exceed the 10/12 limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my company pass a special or unanimous resolution for the buy-back` IF
    (`the s 257B steps for` (`What kind of buy-back is it` `the buy-back`) `over the 10/12 limit`)'s `special or unanimous resolution under s 257D`

@export Must my company lodge the buy-back offer documents with ASIC before the agreement (s 257B table, s 257E)?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
      `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would exceed the 10/12 limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my company lodge the offer documents` IF
    (`the s 257B steps for` (`What kind of buy-back is it` `the buy-back`) `over the 10/12 limit`)'s `lodge offer documents under s 257E`

@export Must my company give ASIC 14 days' notice of the buy-back (s 257B table, s 257F)?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
      `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would exceed the 10/12 limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my company give 14 days notice` IF
    (`the s 257B steps for` (`What kind of buy-back is it` `the buy-back`) `over the 10/12 limit`)'s `14 days notice under s 257F`

@export Must my company send a statement of all material information with the buy-back offer (s 257B table, s 257G)?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
      `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would exceed the 10/12 limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my company disclose the relevant information with the offer` IF
    (`the s 257B steps for` (`What kind of buy-back is it` `the buy-back`) `over the 10/12 limit`)'s `disclose relevant information with the offer under s 257G`

@export Must my company cancel the shares it buys back (s 257B table, s 257H)?
GIVEN `the buy-back` IS A BuyBackFacts @desc How the company proposes to buy back the shares
      `over the 10/12 limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would exceed the 10/12 limit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my company cancel the shares` IF
    (`the s 257B steps for` (`What kind of buy-back is it` `the buy-back`) `over the 10/12 limit`)'s `cancel the shares under s 257H`

-- s 257D(1): the terms "must be approved before it is entered into by either: (a) a special resolution passed at a general
-- meeting of the company, with no votes being cast in favour of the resolution by any person whose shares are proposed to
-- be bought back or by their associates; or (b) a resolution agreed to, at a general meeting, by all ordinary shareholders;
-- or the agreement must be conditional on such an approval." s 250MA(b): a special resolution "must be passed by at least
-- 75% of the votes cast by members who are entitled to vote on the resolution". The seller's votes AGAINST are not barred
-- and count among the votes cast.
@export Is my company's selective buy-back approved by the members under s 257D(1)?
GIVEN `votes for, from members other than the seller and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc Votes cast in favour by members other than the seller and their associates
      `votes for, from the seller or associates` IS A NUMBER @desc Votes cast in favour by the member whose shares are to be bought back, or their associates
      `votes against` IS A NUMBER @desc Votes cast against, from anyone (the seller may vote against)
      `all ordinary shareholders agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every ordinary shareholder agreed to the resolution at a general meeting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the selective buy-back approved` IF
        `all ordinary shareholders agreed`
    OR  (    `votes for, from the seller or associates` EQUALS 0
         AND `votes for, from members other than the seller and associates` TIMES 100 AT LEAST (`votes for, from members other than the seller and associates` PLUS `votes against`) TIMES 75)

-- s 257F(1): the company "must satisfy the lodgment requirement ... at least 14 days before: (a) if the buy-back agreement
-- is conditional on the passing of a resolution under subsection 257C(1) or 257D(1) -- the resolution is passed; or (b) if
-- it is not -- the agreement is entered into." (2): lodging the s 257C(3), 257D(3) or 257E documents, or a notice of intent.
@export Has my company lodged early enough to pass the buy-back resolution or make the agreement on the day planned (s 257F)?
GIVEN `days from lodgment to the resolution or agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from lodging the documents or notice with ASIC to the resolution (or, if none, the agreement)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my company given 14 days notice in time` IF
    `days from lodgment to the resolution or agreement` AT LEAST 14

-- s 257A: "A company may buy back its own shares if: (a) the buy-back does not materially prejudice the company's ability
-- to pay its creditors; and (b) the company follows the procedures laid down in this Division." There is no net-assets
-- test for a buy-back; s 254T is the dividend rule.
@export May my company buy back its own shares (s 257A)?
GIVEN `it materially prejudices paying creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buy-back would materially prejudice the company's ability to pay its creditors
      `the company follows the Division's procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company follows every step the s 257B table requires
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my company buy back its shares` IF
    (NOT `it materially prejudices paying creditors`) AND `the company follows the Division's procedures`

-- s 257H(1): "Once a company has entered into an agreement to buy back shares, all rights attaching to the shares are
-- suspended. The suspension is lifted if the agreement is terminated." (2): "A company must not dispose of shares it buys
-- back. An agreement entered into in contravention of this subsection is void." (3): they are cancelled on registration of
-- the transfer.
@export Do the shares my company has agreed to buy back still carry their rights (s 257H(1))?
GIVEN `the buy-back agreement has been entered into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company has entered into the buy-back agreement
      `the agreement has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that agreement has since been terminated
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the shares still carry their rights` IF
    (NOT `the buy-back agreement has been entered into`) OR `the agreement has been terminated`

§§ `ss 46, 50, 606 -- buying a company, and selling mine`

-- s 46: a body corporate is a subsidiary of another "if, and only if: (a) the other body: (i) controls the composition of
-- the first body's board; or (ii) is in a position to cast, or control the casting of, more than one-half of the maximum
-- number of votes that might be cast at a general meeting of the first body; or (iii) holds more than one-half of the
-- issued share capital of the first body (excluding any part ... that carries no right to participate beyond a specified
-- amount in a distribution of either profits or capital); or (b) the first body is a subsidiary of a subsidiary of the other
-- body." s 50: a holding company, a subsidiary, or "a subsidiary of a holding company of another body corporate" -- "the
-- first-mentioned body and the other body are related to each other". (ss 47 to 49 are not encoded.)
@export Is the company my company has bought into now its subsidiary (s 46)?
GIVEN `my company controls its board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your company controls the composition of the other company's board
      `percent of its votes my company can cast or control` IS A NUMBER @desc Percentage of the maximum votes at the other company's general meeting your company can cast or control
      `percent of its participating share capital my company holds` IS A NUMBER @desc Percentage of the other company's issued share capital (excluding capped-participation shares) your company holds
      `it is a subsidiary of my company's subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a subsidiary of one of your company's subsidiaries
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it my company's subsidiary` IF
        `my company controls its board`
    OR  `percent of its votes my company can cast or control` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `percent of its participating share capital my company holds` GREATER THAN 50
    OR  `it is a subsidiary of my company's subsidiary`

@export Are my company and the other body corporate related bodies corporate (s 50)?
GIVEN `one is the other's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether either is the holding company of the other
      `one is the other's subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether either is a subsidiary of the other
      `one is a subsidiary of the other's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether either is a subsidiary of the other's holding company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are they related bodies corporate` IF
    `one is the other's holding company` OR `one is the other's subsidiary` OR `one is a subsidiary of the other's holding company`

-- s 606(1): "A person must not acquire a relevant interest in issued voting shares in a company if: (a) the company is: (i)
-- a listed company; or (ii) an unlisted company with more than 50 members; and (b) the person acquiring the interest does
-- so through a transaction in relation to securities entered into by or on behalf of the person; and (c) because of the
-- transaction, that person's or someone else's voting power in the company increases: (i) from 20% or below to more than
-- 20%; or (ii) from a starting point that is above 20% and below 90%." (1A): not under a s 611 exception (an INPUT). (3):
-- "count joint holders of a particular parcel of shares as 1 person". Note 3 (effect on another company) is not encoded.
@export Would the buyer's purchase of my company's shares breach the takeovers prohibition (s 606(1))?
GIVEN `the company is listed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company whose shares are bought is listed
      `members of the company, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members the company has
      `it is through a transaction by or for the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer acquires through a transaction in securities entered into by it or on its behalf
      `voting power before, percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The buyer's (or anyone's) voting power before, as a percentage
      `voting power after, percent` IS A NUMBER @desc That voting power after the transaction, as a percentage
      `a s 611 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the exceptions in s 611 applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would the purchase breach the takeovers prohibition` IF
        (`the company is listed` OR `members of the company, joint holders counted as one` GREATER THAN 50)
    AND `it is through a transaction by or for the buyer`
    AND `voting power after, percent` GREATER THAN `voting power before, percent`
    AND (    (`voting power before, percent` AT MOST 20 AND `voting power after, percent` GREATER THAN 20)
         OR  (`voting power before, percent` GREATER THAN 20 AND `voting power before, percent` LESS THAN 90))
    AND (NOT `a s 611 exception applies`)

§§ `ss 674, 674A, 1042A to 1043A -- on a listed company's board`

-- s 1042C(1): information is GENERALLY AVAILABLE if "(a) it consists of readily observable matter; or (b) both ...: (i) it
-- has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly
-- invest in Division 3 financial products of a kind whose price might be affected by the information; and (ii) since it
-- was made known, a reasonable period for it to be disseminated among such persons has elapsed; or (c) it consists of
-- deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from" either.
@export Is the information I hold generally available (s 1042C)?
GIVEN `it is readily observable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is readily observable matter
      `it was made known to those who commonly invest in such products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made known in a way likely to reach people who commonly invest in the affected products
      `a reasonable period to spread has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable period for it to spread among them has since passed
      `it is deduced only from such information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a deduction, conclusion or inference drawn from such information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the information generally available` IF
        `it is readily observable`
    OR  (`it was made known to those who commonly invest in such products` AND `a reasonable period to spread has passed`)
    OR  `it is deduced only from such information`

-- s 1042A(1): "inside information means information in relation to which the following paragraphs are satisfied: (a)
-- the information is not generally available; (b) if the information were generally available -- a reasonable person
-- would expect it to have a material effect on the price or value of particular Division 3 financial products." s 1042D:
-- that is so "if (and only if) the information would, or would be likely to, influence persons who commonly acquire
-- Division 3 financial products in deciding whether or not to acquire or dispose of" them.
@export Is what I know inside information (ss 1042A, 1042D)?
GIVEN `it is generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is generally available (s 1042C)
      `it would likely influence those who commonly acquire such products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it would, or would be likely to, influence people who commonly acquire the products in deciding to buy or sell
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it inside information` IF
    (NOT `it is generally available`) AND `it would likely influence those who commonly acquire such products`

-- s 1043A(1): "Subject to this Subdivision, if: (a) a person (the insider) possesses inside information; and (b) the
-- insider knows, or ought reasonably to know," that it is not generally available and is material, "the insider must not
-- (whether as principal or agent): (c) apply for, acquire, or dispose of, relevant Division 3 financial products, or enter
-- into an agreement to" do so; "or (d) procure another person to" do so. It binds "a person", not only an officer. Nothing
-- in the Act turns on a company's trading window, so it is not asked: an open window does not make dealing lawful.
-- The exceptions in ss 1043B to 1043K (for example s 1043H, a person's knowledge of their own intentions) are one input.
@export Am I forbidden to buy or sell the shares, or to get someone else to, because of what I know (s 1043A(1))?
GIVEN `I possess the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you possess the information
      `it is inside information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is inside information (ss 1042A, 1042D)
      `I know or ought reasonably to know that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know, or ought reasonably to know, it is not generally available and is material
      `an exception in ss 1043B to 1043K applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the exceptions in ss 1043B to 1043K applies to your dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I forbidden to trade` IF
        `I possess the information`
    AND `it is inside information`
    AND `I know or ought reasonably to know that`
    AND (NOT `an exception in ss 1043B to 1043K applies`)

-- s 1043A(2): if the insider possesses inside information, knows or ought reasonably to know it is such, "and (c) relevant
-- Division 3 financial products are able to be traded on a financial market operated in this jurisdiction; the insider
-- must not, directly or indirectly, communicate the information, or cause the information to be communicated, to another
-- person if the insider knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the other person would or would be likely to" deal or
-- procure.
@export Am I forbidden to pass on what I know (s 1043A(2))?
GIVEN `I possess the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you possess the information
      `it is inside information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is inside information (ss 1042A, 1042D)
      `I know or ought reasonably to know that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know, or ought reasonably to know, it is not generally available and is material
      `the products can be traded on an Australian financial market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the shares or other products can be traded on a financial market operated in this jurisdiction
      `I know or ought to know they would likely deal or procure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know, or ought reasonably to know, the person told would be likely to deal or get someone else to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I forbidden to pass it on` IF
        `I possess the information`
    AND `it is inside information`
    AND `I know or ought reasonably to know that`
    AND `the products can be traded on an Australian financial market`
    AND `I know or ought to know they would likely deal or procure`

-- s 674(2): if the listing rules require the entity to notify, "(b) the entity has information that those provisions
-- require the entity to notify ...; and (c) the information is not generally available; and (d) a reasonable person would
-- expect the information, if it were generally available, to have a material effect on the price or value of ED
-- securities of the entity; the entity must notify the market operator". The duty is the ENTITY's, not the director's.
@export Must the listed company I am a director of tell the market (s 674(2))?
GIVEN `the listing rules require it to be notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the listing rules require the company to notify the market operator of the information
      `it is generally available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is generally available
      `a reasonable person would expect a material effect on price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person would expect it, if generally available, to materially affect the price of the company's securities
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the listed company tell the market` IF
        `the listing rules require it to be notified`
    AND (NOT `it is generally available`)
    AND `a reasonable person would expect a material effect on price`

-- s 674A(3): "A person who is involved in a listed disclosing entity's contravention of subsection (2) contravenes this
-- subsection." s 674A(2) is s 674(2) with a fault element: the entity "knows, or is reckless or negligent with respect to
-- whether" the information is material. (4): not if the person proves they "(a) took all steps (if any) that were
-- reasonable in the circumstances to ensure that the listed disclosing entity complied ...; and (b) after doing so,
-- believed on reasonable grounds that the listed disclosing entity was complying". A director is caught only this way.
@export Am I personally liable for the listed company's failure to disclose (s 674A(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the company contravened s 674A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company failed to notify information it knew, or was reckless or negligent about, was material
      `I was involved in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were involved in it (aided, induced, were knowingly concerned in it, and so on)
      `I took all reasonable steps to ensure it complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you took all steps that were reasonable to ensure the company complied
      `I then believed on reasonable grounds it was complying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after that, you believed on reasonable grounds it was complying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable for the failure to disclose` IF
        `the company contravened s 674A(2)`
    AND `I was involved in the contravention`
    AND (NOT (`I took all reasonable steps to ensure it complied` AND `I then believed on reasonable grounds it was complying`))
